### PayVerse — api-gateway smoke checks (IntelliJ HTTP Client / VS Code REST Client)
# Select environment "local" (http/http-client.env.json). Requests for each service are added per phase.

### Liveness / readiness probes (public)
GET {{gateway}}/actuator/health/liveness

###
GET {{gateway}}/actuator/health/readiness

### Protected route without a token → 401 application/problem+json with correlationId
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/wallets/me
X-Correlation-Id: http-demo-001

### Internal endpoints are never routed by the gateway → 401/403
GET {{gateway}}/internal/wallets/123

### OTP route: public, limited to 5 requests/minute per IP.
# Until auth-service exists (Phase 2) this returns 503 DOWNSTREAM_UNAVAILABLE from the circuit-breaker fallback.
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/auth/otp/request
Content-Type: application/json

{ "mobile": "{{mobile}}" }

### CORS preflight from an allowed origin
OPTIONS {{gateway}}/api/v1/wallets/me
Origin: http://localhost:3000
Access-Control-Request-Method: POST
Access-Control-Request-Headers: Authorization,Idempotency-Key

### Aggregated Swagger UI (each service's docs appear as it comes online)
GET {{gateway}}/swagger-ui.html
